#: commands/batch-lr-unit.md:9
msgid "Read many land registry units at once"
msgstr ""

#: commands/batch-lr-unit.md:11
msgid ""
"Give the tool a list of land registry units, or the result of a [batch-"
"fetch](batch-fetch.md) run, and it prints the sheets of every unit one after "
"another."
msgstr ""

#: commands/batch-lr-unit.md:17
msgid ""
"You have checked a list of parcels with batch-fetch and now want the owners "
"and encumbrances of each."
msgstr ""

#: commands/batch-lr-unit.md:18
msgid ""
"You keep a list of units for a case and want to re-read all of them after a "
"change."
msgstr ""

#: commands/batch-lr-unit.md:22
msgid ""
"Each unit is identified by its number and the main book ID. The easiest way "
"to get both is the JSON file that [batch-fetch](batch-fetch.md) writes. You "
"can also prepare a CSV file with two columns, `lr_unit_number` and "
"`main_book_id`, like the example [lr_units.csv](../examples/lr_units.csv):"
msgstr ""

#: commands/batch-lr-unit.md:36
msgid "Open Terminal in the folder where your file is."
msgstr ""

