#: commands/cache-clear.md:9
msgid "Remove stored boundary data"
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:11
msgid ""
"Deletes the boundary data of one municipality, or of all of them, from your "
"computer. The tool downloads the data again the next time you ask for a "
"boundary."
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:17
msgid ""
"The boundaries of a municipality have changed and you want the tool to fetch "
"the current data."
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:18
msgid "You want to free disk space."
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:22
msgid ""
"Decide whether you want to remove one municipality or all of them. Nothing "
"else is affected: the stored data is only a copy of what the server can send "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:29
msgid ""
"Type the following line and press Enter. Replace SAVAR with the municipality "
"you want to remove."
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:44
msgid "The tool confirms what it removed and how much space it freed."
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:48
msgid ""
"`--force` skips the question the tool otherwise asks before deleting. Without"
" it, the tool asks you to confirm; type `y` and press Enter to go ahead, or "
"just press Enter to keep the data."
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:52
msgid "To remove everything, use `--all` instead of naming a municipality:"
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:68
msgid ""
"If you name a municipality that is not stored, the tool tells you so and "
"removes nothing:"
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:77
msgid "If you name neither a municipality nor `--all`, you will see this:"
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:89
msgid "[cache-list](cache-list.md) shows what is stored before you remove it."
msgstr ""

#: commands/cache-clear.md:90
msgid "[download-gis](download-gis.md) downloads a municipality again."
msgstr ""

