msgid "[Start here](../start-here.md) is the tutorial."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:9
msgid "List the cadastral municipalities of an office"
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:11
msgid ""
"Shows the cadastral municipalities with their registration numbers, filtered "
"by cadastral office, by department, or by part of a name."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:16
msgid ""
"You work with one cadastral office and want the numbers of all its "
"municipalities on one sheet."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:17
msgid ""
"You want to check which department a municipality belongs to before you "
"contact the office."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:21
msgid ""
"You need the number of the cadastral office. The [list-offices](list-"
"offices.md) page shows all of them."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:63
msgid ""
"**Code** is the number to give after `-m` in the other commands. The first "
"line tells you how many municipalities the office has."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:68
msgid ""
"Add `--department` to narrow the list to one department of the office, or "
"`--search` with part of a name to look for one municipality:"
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:75
msgid ""
"Without any filter the tool lists every municipality it knows, which is a "
"long list. Add `--count-only` to get only the number, or `--format csv` with "
"`--output` to keep the list as a spreadsheet file."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:92
msgid "If the office number is wrong, you will see this:"
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:100
msgid ""
"Check the number on the [list-offices](list-offices.md) page. Other messages "
"are explained on the [errors page](../errors.md)."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:105
msgid "[search-municipality](search-municipality.md) searches by name."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-municipalities.md:106
msgid "[list-offices](list-offices.md) gives the office numbers."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-offices.md:9
msgid "List the cadastral offices"
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-offices.md:11
msgid ""
"Shows every regional cadastral office (područni ured za katastar) with its "
"number. You need the number to list the municipalities of an office."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-offices.md:16
msgid "You want to know which office is responsible for an area."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-offices.md:17
msgid "Another command asks for an office number and you do not know it."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-offices.md:21
msgid "Nothing. This command takes no input."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-offices.md:74
msgid ""
"**ID** is the office number. Use it with `--office` on the [list-"
"municipalities](list-municipalities.md) page."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-offices.md:79
msgid ""
"To keep the list as a file, add `--format csv` and `--output` with a file "
"name:"
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-offices.md:94
msgid ""
"This command only fails when the tool cannot reach the practice server. The "
"message is explained on the [errors page](../errors.md); ask the person who "
"installed the tool to start the server."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-offices.md:100
msgid "[list-municipalities](list-municipalities.md) uses the office number."
msgstr ""

#: commands/list-offices.md:101
msgid "[info](info.md) shows which server the tool is talking to."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:9
msgid "Find the number of a cadastral municipality"
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:11
msgid ""
"Every cadastral municipality (katastarska općina, k.o.) has a registration "
"number. This command finds it from the name, or lists the municipalities that"
" belong to a cadastral office."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:17
msgid ""
"Two municipalities have the same or a similar name and you want to be sure "
"which one you are looking at."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:18
msgid ""
"A command refused the municipality name and you need the number instead."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:19
msgid ""
"You want to know which cadastral office (područni ured za katastar) and "
"department a municipality belongs to."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:23
msgid "You need the name of the municipality, or part of it."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:48
msgid ""
"**Code** is the registration number you can give to any other command after "
"`-m`. **Office** and **Department** are the numbers of the cadastral office "
"and its department."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:54
msgid ""
"To list every municipality of one office, give the office number with "
"`--office`. You can combine it with a name to narrow the list:"
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:61
msgid ""
"If you only want to know how many municipalities match, add `--count-only`. "
"To keep the list as a file, add `--format csv` and `--output` with a file "
"name."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:77
msgid "If nothing matches, you will see this:"
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:85
msgid ""
"Try a shorter part of the name, or list the whole office with `--office` and "
"look for the name in the list. Other messages are explained on the [errors "
"page](../errors.md)."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:91
msgid ""
"[list-municipalities](list-municipalities.md) does the same job with a "
"different set of filters."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:92
msgid ""
"[list-offices](list-offices.md) shows the office numbers to use with "
"`--office`."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search-municipality.md:93
msgid "[search](search.md) is where you use the number you found."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:9
msgid "Check a parcel quickly"
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:11
msgid ""
"Type a parcel number and the cadastral municipality, and get the basics on "
"one screen: where the parcel is, how big it is, what the land is used for, "
"and how many people the cadastre records on it."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:17
msgid ""
"A client mentions a parcel and you want to confirm it exists before you go "
"any further."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:18
msgid ""
"You need the area and the land use of a parcel for a contract or a valuation."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:19
msgid ""
"You want the registration number of the municipality and the parcel's "
"internal number for a later, more detailed lookup."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:23
msgid ""
"You need two things: the parcel number (broj katastarske čestice, for example"
" 103/2) and the cadastral municipality (katastarska općina) it belongs to. "
"Both are on any extract from the cadastre or the land registry, and on most "
"contracts."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:27
msgid ""
"You can give the municipality by name (SAVAR) or by its registration number "
"(334979). The tool accepts either."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:55
msgid ""
"Read the lines from top to bottom. **Parcel Number** and **Municipality** "
"confirm that the tool found the parcel you meant. **Area** is the surface in "
"square metres. **Land Use** is the cadastral culture, in the wording of the "
"cadastre. **Building Permitted** tells you whether building is allowed on the"
" parcel according to the cadastre. **Possessors** is the number of people the"
" cadastre records on the parcel. They are possessors (posjednici), not "
"necessarily the legal owners; the land registry has those."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:63
msgid ""
"The last line suggests the command for the full details. Copy it if you need "
"more than this summary."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:68
msgid ""
"The part after `-m` is the municipality. It can be a name or a number. If two"
" municipalities share a name, use the number, which you can find with "
"[search-municipality](search-municipality.md)."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:72
msgid ""
"If you only know the beginning of a parcel number, add `--partial` to see "
"every parcel that starts with what you typed:"
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:79
msgid ""
"To keep the result as a file instead of reading it on screen, add `--format "
"json` or `--format csv` and `--output` with a file name. A JSON file can be "
"read by other programs; a CSV file opens in a spreadsheet."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:99
msgid ""
"If the parcel number does not exist in that municipality, the tool says so "
"and stops:"
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:107
msgid ""
"Check the number on your document. Parcel numbers often contain a slash, and "
"103 is not the same parcel as 103/2."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:110
msgid ""
"If the municipality is not recognised, the message names it. Check the "
"spelling, or use the number instead. Other messages are explained on the "
"[errors page](../errors.md)."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:116
msgid ""
"[get-parcel](get-parcel.md) shows everything the cadastre holds about the "
"parcel, including the recorded possessors."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:117
msgid ""
"[get-lr-unit](get-lr-unit.md) shows the land registry unit: owners, shares "
"and encumbrances."
msgstr ""

#: commands/search.md:118
msgid ""
"[search-municipality](search-municipality.md) finds the number of a cadastral"
" municipality."
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:9
msgid "What the error messages mean"
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:11
msgid ""
"When something goes wrong, the tool stops and prints one line in red. This "
"page lists the messages and says what to do about each."
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:33
msgid "Messages about what you typed"
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:35
msgid ""
"**Parcel not found** means the parcel number does not exist in the "
"municipality you named. Check the number on your document, including the part"
" after the slash, and check that you named the right municipality."
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:39
msgid ""
"**Municipality not found** means the name or number after `-m` is not known. "
"Check the spelling, or find the registration number with [search-"
"municipality](commands/search-municipality.md) and use that instead."
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:43
msgid ""
"**Land registry unit not found** means the unit number and main book you gave"
" do not match a unit. Check both numbers. If you started from a parcel, the "
"parcel may not be entered in the land registry yet."
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:47
msgid "Messages about the connection"
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:49
msgid ""
"**Connection error** means the tool could not reach the server. For practice "
"use, the practice server on your computer is not running. Ask the person who "
"installed the tool to start it, then run the command again."
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:53
msgid ""
"**Request timed out** means the server did not answer in time. Wait a moment "
"and run the command again."
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:56
msgid ""
"**Rate limit exceeded** means requests were sent too quickly. The tool "
"already spaces its requests; wait a minute and try again."
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:59
msgid ""
"**Server error** and **Invalid response from server** mean the server "
"answered but not in the expected way. Try again later. If it keeps happening,"
" tell the person who installed the tool."
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:63
msgid "Messages from Terminal itself"
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:65
msgid ""
"If Terminal answers `command not found`, the tool is not installed for your "
"account or Terminal was opened before the installation finished. Close "
"Terminal, open it again, and retry. If it still fails, ask the person who "
"installed the tool."
msgstr ""

#: errors.md:70
msgid ""
"If the tool prints `Missing option` or `No such option`, part of the command "
"is misspelt. Compare your line with the example on the command's page."
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:9
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:11
msgid ""
"The words of the cadastre and the land registry, and where the tool shows "
"each of them. Croatian terms are given as they appear on official documents."
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:14
msgid "| Term | What it means | Where you see it in the tool |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:16
msgid ""
"| Katastarska čestica (k.č.) | A parcel: one numbered piece of land in the "
"cadastre. | The parcel number you type after `search`, `get-parcel` and `get-"
"geometry`. |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:17
msgid ""
"| Katastarska općina (k.o.) | The cadastral municipality a parcel belongs to."
" Each has a name and a registration number (matični broj), which the tool "
"prints as its code. | The value after `-m` in most commands. [search-"
"municipality](commands/search-municipality.md) finds the number. |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:18
msgid ""
"| Posjedovni list | The possession sheet of the cadastre: who possesses a "
"parcel according to the cadastre. Not proof of ownership. | [get-"
"parcel](commands/get-parcel.md) with `--show-owners`. |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:19
msgid ""
"| Posjednik | A possessor recorded in the cadastre. | The rows of the "
"possession sheet on [get-parcel](commands/get-parcel.md). |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:20
msgid ""
"| Zemljišnoknjižni uložak (ZK uložak) | The land registry unit: the record of"
" the legal state of a property, kept by the land registry department of the "
"municipal court. | [get-lr-unit](commands/get-lr-unit.md). Its number also "
"appears on [get-parcel](commands/get-parcel.md) and in the batch results. |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:21
msgid ""
"| Glavna knjiga | The main book: the volume of the land registry that holds "
"the units of one cadastral municipality. | `--main-book` on [get-lr-"
"unit](commands/get-lr-unit.md). |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:22
msgid ""
"| Posjedovnica (list A) | Sheet A: the parcels that make up the unit. | The "
"first table after the unit header on [get-lr-unit](commands/get-lr-unit.md). "
"|"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:23
msgid ""
"| Vlastovnica (list B) | Sheet B: the owners and their shares. | `--show-"
"owners` on [get-lr-unit](commands/get-lr-unit.md). |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:24
msgid ""
"| Teretovnica (list C) | Sheet C: liens (mortgages), easements, real burdens "
"and notes. | `--show-encumbrances` on [get-lr-unit](commands/get-lr-unit.md)."
" |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:25
msgid ""
"| Suvlasnički udio | A co-ownership share, written as a fraction such as 1/2."
" | The share column of sheet B. |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:26
msgid ""
"| Plomba | A mark that a request for registration (prijedlog za upis) has "
"been received and not yet decided. The unit may change. | The pending entries"
" line on [get-lr-unit](commands/get-lr-unit.md); `--plombe-detail` shows what"
" each request is. |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:27
msgid ""
"| Dnevnik, broj Z | The diary of the land registry and the file number "
"(Z-number) of a request for registration. | The last diary number on [get-lr-"
"unit](commands/get-lr-unit.md) and the file numbers of the pending entries. |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:28
msgid ""
"| Etažno vlasništvo | Ownership of a special part of a property (a flat or "
"business premises), tied to a co-ownership share of the whole. | The unit "
"type row of the unit header on [get-lr-unit](commands/get-lr-unit.md). |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:29
msgid ""
"| Kultura, način uporabe zemljišta | The land use recorded in the cadastre, "
"such as arable land, pasture or orchard. | The land use table on [get-"
"parcel](commands/get-parcel.md). |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:30
msgid ""
"| OIB | The personal identification number of a natural or legal person. | "
"The OIB column of sheet B, when the registry has it. |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:31
msgid ""
"| Područni ured za katastar | A regional cadastral office. | [list-"
"offices](commands/list-offices.md). |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:32
msgid ""
"| Granica čestice | The boundary of a parcel as coordinates. | [get-"
"geometry](commands/get-geometry.md) and [download-gis](commands/download-"
"gis.md). |"
msgstr ""

#: glossary.md:33
msgid ""
"| HTRS96/TM (EPSG:3765) | The official coordinate system of Croatia, used for"
" all boundaries. | Every coordinate the tool prints. |"
msgstr ""

